<article class="env-lemma" id="0GQH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GQH">Lemma <span data-tag="0GQH">103.8.3</span>.</a> Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a morphism of algebraic stacks which is quasi-compact, quasi-separated, and representable by algebraic spaces. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be in $\textit{LQCoh}^{fbc}(\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X})$. Then for an object $y : V \to \mathcal{Y}$ of $\mathcal{Y}$ we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (R^ if_*\mathcal{F})|_{V_{\acute{e}tale}} = R^ if'_{small, *}(\mathcal{F}|_{U_{\acute{e}tale}})  \]
</div>
  <p> where $f' : U = V \times _\mathcal {Y} \mathcal{X} \to V$ is the base change of $f$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Sheaves on Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/075H" data-tag="075H">96.21.3</a> we can reduce to the case where $\mathcal{X}$ is represented by $U$ and $\mathcal{Y}$ is represented by $V$. Of course this also uses that the pullback of $\mathcal{F}$ to $U$ is in $\textit{LQCoh}^{fbc}(\mathcal{O}_ U)$ by Proposition <a href="/tag/0771" data-tag="0771">103.8.1</a>. Then the result follows from Sheaves on Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/075N" data-tag="075N">96.22.2</a> and the fact that $R^ if_*$ may be computed in the étale topology by Proposition <a href="/tag/0771" data-tag="0771">103.8.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>